            </div>
        </div>
<div class="my-2" data-zesty-id="design:design:whitespace-sm:17:99"></div>
<div class="row my-3" data-zesty-id="design:columns:2columnswideright:28:71">
<div class="col-md-4 col-sm-12" data-zesty-id="design:columns:2columnswideright:28:71-2:2 Columns - Left Small:0">
<img src="https://s3.amazonaws.com/uss-cache.salvationarmy.org/fa4e4917-37ba-4e18-be87-fa345000e4fe_Camp%2Bphoto%2B2.jpeg" alt="placeholder" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;" loading="lazy" class="img-fluid d-block my-3 rounded mx-auto" data-zesty-id="content:images:20:79">
				</div>
<div class="col-md-8 col-sm-12" data-zesty-id="design:columns:2columnswideright:28:71-4:2 Columns - Left Small:1">
<h5 data-zesty-id="content:text:22:54">Summer Camp&nbsp;</h5>
<p data-zesty-id="content:textarea:23:73">
					Many children leave school each spring and head out for a fun-filled summer of camps. However, for many kids from income-limited homes, the possibility of going to summer camp is not an option.&nbsp;
				</p>
<p data-zesty-id="content:textarea:24:55">
					We believe every child should experience summer camp—exploring nature, learning new skills, developing confidence, and building life-long friendships in a fun and nurturing environment. That’s Why we offer kids from across Alabama, Louisiana, and Mississippi to experience one or more summer camp programs at Camp Hidden Lake, our 300-acre camp in Lexington, Mississippi.
				</p>
<p data-zesty-id="content:textarea:25:92">
					Camp Hidden Lake is residential for a week (6 days), and transportation is provided. During the week, campers experience long, hot summer days, dips in the pool, star-filled nights, campfires, roasted marshmallows, pillow fights, cabin devotions, emblem work, seeing old friends, and making new ones.
				</p>
<p style="text-align:center;" data-zesty-id="content:wysiwyg_basic:26:95">
					For more information, &nbsp;call <a href="tel:+12253554483" target="">225-355-4483</a> x.401
				</p>
				</div>
			</div>
<div class="my-2" data-zesty-id="design:design:whitespace-sm:29:50"></div>
